Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 08:32:44 2026 +0400

    Use MLXLogger for the model component warning (#790)
    
    #711 added a warning in ModelComponent.swift through `Logger(subsystem:category:)`.
    When its CI ran on Oct 19, MLXLMCommon/Linux/Logger.swift still declared
    `typealias Logger = os.Logger` for the whole module, so the file compiled
    without importing os. #702 then deleted that alias and moved the libraries to
    MLXLogger. #711 merged on Nov 10 with the checks from before #702, so main no
    longer builds:
    
        ModelComponent.swift:28:22: error: cannot find 'Logger' in scope
    
    Use `MLXLogger(label:)`, like every other logger in the libraries since #702.
    Importing os would also build, but it fails on Linux and skips the backend that
    apps install through `MLXLogger.factory`.

