commit a8429d0f370e27ad73dbe2fb80afb2c864df3861
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 21:17:38 2026 +0400

    Measure the memory of an EmbeddingGemma 2 embedding (#787)
    
    `ModelContainer` and `EmbedderModelContainer` report the buffers of their
    model through `ModelMemoryReporting`, but `EmbeddingGemma2Embedding` keeps its
    model private and reports nothing. An application that shows what each loaded
    model holds cannot measure this embedder, and its vision and audio encoders,
    which load the first time an input needs them, stay invisible too.
    
    Conform `EmbeddingGemma2Embedding` to `ModelMemoryReporting`. `memory()`
    returns the model's own `memory()`, so a media encoder counts once it has
    loaded, as it does for a VLM in a `ModelContainer`.
    
    `MultimodalEmbedding` itself does not require it: the protocol is public, and
    adding a requirement would break every other conformer.

