commit 4ab267996c83a1ae60789850cddfe646043cc36d
Author: xocialize <dustin.nielson@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 13:05:43 2026 -0800

    MLXVLM Qwen35: apply YaRN from rope_parameters on the VLM rotary (#761)
    
    The VLM rotary built plain M-RoPE and ignored rope_parameters, so a
    Qwen3.5 checkpoint with rope_type "yarn" ran with default frequencies and
    no attention factor. MLXLLM Qwen35 already applies YaRN through
    initializeRope.
    
    RotaryEmbedding now computes inv_freq and the attention factor like HF
    `_compute_yarn_parameters` when the type is "yarn", and scales cos and
    sin by that factor. This scales only the rotary slice of q and k, as HF
    does. Other rope types take the old path unchanged.
    A missing original_max_position_embeddings falls back to
    max_position_embeddings, as HF does.
    
    On sensenova/SenseNova-6.8-Code2Video (factor 2, original 262144),
    YaRN changes 17 of 32 rotary frequencies and the factor is 1.0693. 8-bit
    text-position KL against HF bf16 over a 988-token prompt drops from
    0.051 to 0.016.
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

