commit 37424a526e9211c64ac431e283f82c1d8c9e1d79
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 22:24:07 2026 +0400

    Stop image prompts from running VLM language models in float32 (#766)
    
    * Keep Qwen2-VL and Qwen2.5-VL in the model dtype on image prompts
    
    The M-RoPE path rotates queries and keys with float32 cos and sin, so
    image prompts promote them to float32. Layer 0 caches float32 keys
    beside float16 values and returns a float32 attention output. From
    there every layer runs and caches in float32. Decode reads twice the
    KV bytes, and SDPA casts layer 0's values on every step.
    
    Cast cos and sin to the hidden-state dtype, as mlx-vlm does and as
    Qwen3VL and Qwen3.5 already do here. Text-only prompts take the plain
    RoPE path and do not change.
    
    A regression test runs a float16 tiny model through an image prefill
    and one decode step. It checks that every cache layer stays float16.
    
    * Keep FastVLM and Mistral3 image features in the model dtype
    
    FastVLM passed float32 pixels to its vision tower, so the image
    features came out float32. Concatenating them with the text embeddings
    promoted the whole language model and its KV cache to float32. Cast
    the pixels to the patch-embed weight dtype, as mlx-vlm does.
    
    Mistral3 cast its image features to bfloat16 before the patch merger.
    For a float16 checkpoint this mixed bfloat16 and float16, which
    promoted the language model to float32 in the same way. The Pixtral
    tower already returns features in its weight dtype, so drop the cast,
    as mlx-vlm does. bfloat16 checkpoints do not change.
    
    A parameterized test runs each tiny VLM in that suite in float16
    through an image prefill and one decode step, and checks the cache
    dtype.

