commit 0dabaf794ff84d33208f9e934efb13ed12ba337f
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 21:34:25 2026 +0400

    Add production-ready LFM2.5 model support (#528)
    
    * Add production-ready LFM2.5 model support
    
    Support dense and MoE LFM2.5 checkpoints, including mixed-precision quantization, causal hybrid caches, reasoning/tool conventions, and scoped model variants. Harden model subdirectory resolution and add strict real-checkpoint and regression coverage.
    
    * Add LFM2.5 DSpark speculative decoding
    
    * Optimize quantized MoE route grouping
    
    * MLXVLM: fail closed when the LFM2VL image token cannot be resolved
    
    #576 replaced the hardcoded 396 with a vocabulary lookup but kept 396 as
    the fallback. That fallback is wrong for the LFM2.5 vocabulary, where id
    396 is the ordinary BPE token "ab": a tokenizer without an `<image>`
    entry makes the processor scan prose for markers instead of reporting the
    problem, and the model then aborts the host process.
    
    The processor now resolves the id once in `init` and throws from `prepare`
    when the vocabulary has no such token. `mergeInputIdsWithImageFeatures`
    throws instead of calling `fatalError`, so a disagreement between the
    tokenizer-derived marker and `config.json`'s `image_token_id` is catchable
    and names both ids rather than killing the process with no crash report.
    
    Also removes the duplicated magic values. The placeholder text becomes
    `LFM2VLProcessorConfiguration.imageToken`, overridable via `image_token`
    as Pixtral, Mistral3 and MuseGlimmer already do, and the legacy 396
    default now lives only in `LFM2VLConfiguration.defaultImageTokenId`.
    
    * Load LFM2VL vision on demand and harden LFM loading and cache rewinds

